{"id":14117,"artist":"H.G. Spafford & P.P. Bliss","title":"When Peace, Like A River","lyrics_plain":null,"lyrics_synced":"[00:02.07] When peace, like a river,\n[00:07.59] attendeth my way,\n[00:13.10] When sorrows, like seabillows, roll\n[00:24.14] Whatever my lot,\n[00:28.97] thou hast taught me to say,\n[00:34.48] It is well, it is well with my soul.\n[00:45.52] It is well (It is well) with my soul (with my soul)\n[00:56.55] It is well, it is well with my soul\n[01:08.28] Though Satan should buffet,\n[01:13.79] though trials should come,\n[01:19.31] Let this blest assurance control\n[01:30.34] That Christ hath regarded my helpless estate,\n[01:40.69] And hath shed His own blood for my soul.\n[01:51.72] It is well (It is well) with my soul (with my soul)\n[02:02.76] It is well, it is well with my soul.\n[02:14.48] My sin, O the bliss of this glorious tho't!\n[02:25.52] My sin, not in part but the whole\n[02:36.55] Is nailed to his cross,\n[02:41.38] and I bear it no more; Praise the Lord, praise the Lord,\n[02:52.41] O my soul!\n[02:57.93] It is well (It is well) with my soul (with my soul)\n[03:08.97] It is well, it is well with my soul.\n","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:02.06] <00:02.06>When <00:02.75>peace, <00:04.13>like <00:04.82>a <00:05.51>ri <00:06.89>ver,\n[00:07.58] <00:07.58>at <00:08.27>tend <00:09.65>eth <00:10.34>my <00:11.03>way,\n[00:13.10] <00:13.10>When <00:13.79>sor <00:15.17>rows, <00:15.86>like <00:16.55>sea <00:17.93>bil <00:18.62>lows, <00:19.31>roll <00:22.06>;\n[00:24.13] <00:24.13>What <00:24.82>ev <00:26.20>er <00:26.89>my <00:27.58>lot,\n[00:28.96] <00:28.96>thou <00:29.65>hast <00:30.34>taught <00:31.72>me <00:32.41>to <00:33.10>say,\n[00:34.48] <00:34.48>It <00:35.17>is <00:35.86>well, <00:37.24>it <00:37.93>is <00:38.62>well <00:39.99>with <00:41.03>my <00:41.37>soul.\n[00:45.51] <00:45.51>It <00:46.20>is <00:46.89>well <00:48.27>(It <00:48.96>is <00:49.65>well) <00:51.03>with <00:51.72>my <00:52.41>soul <00:53.79>(with <00:54.48>my <0